{
 "about": [
  "Shared file-call cases every client runs through its own checked file call (internal/clientcases,",
  "path files-call): Go's Session.RunFiles, Python's Session.run_files, TypeScript's",
  "Session.runFiles, each against the files daemon of internal/clientsuite (files.go), which is the",
  "real RPC handler over sessions whose file calls an in-memory work folder answers. Each case is",
  "one session, opened fresh, and its calls in order. A call names its operation and its fields in",
  "a form no client uses itself: paths, contents, globs and cursors in hex, so a name that is not",
  "UTF-8 or holds a newline is written exactly; scope is work. forge names the forged answer the",
  "daemon gives (clientsuite.FilesForgeries, asked by the trace ID forge-files-<name>).",
  "expect: per call, the answer as each client returned it (outcome, error and errno by their",
  "words, op the answer's operation or \"\" for none, its fields with bytes in hex), or the",
  "refusal: refused is not_dispatched:<reason> or may_have_run, and check, given where the call",
  "says rule, the kind of rule that refused it (a client whose errors name no kind is compared",
  "without it). Ids are never reused: a retired case's id moves to retired."
 ],
